Subject: [PATCH] test(kanban): snapshot synced backfill homes per module
 [daveey]

Why: the original 168-case file spends most of its time rebuilding real
SessionDB and synced Kanban schemas. Eleven representative cases spent
11.110s in make_home versus 0.268s in test calls. Under the frozen G39
1818-file/16-worker load, unchanged main bb4d3d72 took 396.8s (168 pass).
The independently landed empty-session-schema optimization at 192d1786
still took 309.6s (170 pass), exceeding the unchanged 300s acceptance.

Build the real synced home once and snapshot each SQLite database using
backup, including committed WAL pages. Deep-copy the complete fixture
per case and reapply the original home/worker isolation. Backfill still
runs against real independent on-disk schemas. Keep all original test
functions/decorators/assertions, including the landed empty-session
isolation checks. Add fresh-make_home schema parity and independent
session/board mutation controls. No production, selection, retries or
watchdog changes; no skip, xfail, move or split.

Proof: canonical serial run: 171 passed in 73.3s, retries 0.
Hardlink-copy mutant: baseline 3 passed; mutant 2 failed/1 passed.
All 53 pre-optimization tests AST-identical; scripts/check passes.
Matched frozen1818/j16/retries0 proof is tracked on the implementation
card and must be under300 before completion.

Implementation: t_a67f352e2a028f7a
